</div>
<div>
<div class="faq-list"><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>Does it actually mop well?</summary><p class="faq-answer">It can help maintain hard floors between deeper cleans. It should not be treated as a full replacement for occasional manual mopping.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>How loud is a robot vacuum?</summary><p class="faq-answer">The vacuum itself is noticeable but usually tolerable. The self-empty dock is much louder for a short burst when it empties the bin.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>Will it pick up pet hair on carpet?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Yes, but performance depends on carpet height, hair length, and how often it runs. Robot vacuums work best when they clean frequently rather than waiting for heavy buildup.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>How often does the dock need maintenance?</summary><p class="faq-answer">You still need to empty or replace bags, refill water, clean mop components, and check brushes. The dock reduces chores; it does not eliminate them.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>Is the app necessary?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Yes, for setup, mapping, scheduling, room control, and maintenance alerts. After setup, most people can keep daily use fairly simple.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>When should I spend less?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Spend less if you mostly need vacuuming, have manageable rugs, and do not need a full wash/refill mop dock. A vacuum-first self-emptying model can be the better value.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>When should I spend more?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Spend more only if your home has difficult thresholds, mixed rugs, or you genuinely need stronger automated mopping. Otherwise, premium dock features can add cost and maintenance without changing the daily result enough.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What matters more: suction or navigation?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Navigation often matters more. High suction does not help much if the robot misses rooms, gets stuck, or cleans inefficiently.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Should I run it every day?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Frequent cleaning is usually the point. Running it often keeps dirt and pet hair from building up and makes each cleaning session easier.</p></details>
</div>
